  "body": "## Scientific scope\nSuccessor to byte-pinned bass_cr C18 `a6678e50b4d284e3188a74229a47736611f92d91`; owner `rei_bianchi@0fcb2dddf5de6b583c2e00f150abff0b2afb6315` read-only, 18/18 SHA-256 file identities independently checked. Actual 8 rays x 49 energies original Rust checkpoints, native source injection and native Verner sigma; no invented photon source and R/J applied once.\n\nConstructed positive exact exponential frozen-endpoint-opacity photon source/absorption per proper timestep, species-resolved H/He ionization and photoheat, coupled four-variable damped backward-Euler solve using the **original Rust** `igm_thermal::igm_point_rhs` (CI, RR, DR, CMB, thermal Case-A). Bookkeeping keeps physical binding thresholds separate from Verner fit cutoffs; checks photon-number, spectral-energy, chemical binding, thermal gas, escaping radiation and CMB reservoir ledgers.\n\n## Execution evidence\nCompiled original owner-linked Rust bridge on user Ubuntu workstation; 12/12 fresh Python tests PASS (`TEST_RECEIPT.log`), ZERO and SHEAR_PLUS genuine AXBI sources at **different physical epochs**, exact gas positivity/ledger tests, source-free/invalid-state controls, one-step vs two half-steps. Proper dt=1e9..1e12s bounded study yields max local total-energy ledger residual 4.621e-16 eV/H, endpoint-vs-frozen photoevent relative feedback 0.02185% (ZERO) and 0.04000% (SHEAR_PLUS). Source identities + machine results in `research/cr_c19_coupled_20261015/`.\n\n**Do not merge with owner production**: this is a bounded static-epoch, fixed-energy and fixed-source model, not a common-time Bianchi anisotropy comparison, OTS/Case B chemistry, time-resolved source-age transfer, validated FLRW cosmological history or a numerical error certificate. `rei_bianchi` PR150's newer covariant-q ref transport and isotope path requires independent native comparison. All full EoR gates HOLD. AOCC capture NO_GO remains unchanged. NCP64 root SSH publickey auth failed; no heavy NCP computation claimed. No native subagents available. Separate dual cloud source/backup receipt forthcoming, not a condition for reviewing the code.",
